WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:03.033
-James Spader,
welcome back to our program.

00:00:03.033 --> 00:00:04.400
It's always great
to have you on.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.434
I was telling you that
we're playing a segment called

00:00:06.434 --> 00:00:09.467
"Do Not Play" with weird songs,
and you go,

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.968
"Yeah, I have this song
that haunts me."

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:14.100
-A whole record, actually.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:18.501
I -- It was a --
Should I show it here?

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.567
-Yeah. Show the --

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:21.067
-So, this is what
the cover looks like.

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:22.167
-Yeah.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:23.667
-So...
-Yeah, let me see it. So...

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:28.467
-So, it's Mother Goose
nursery rhymes, right?

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:30.501
-That's a little frightening
right there.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.334
-But -- And I grew up
with these.

00:00:32.334 --> 00:00:35.734
And I must tell you,
I am like the third child.

00:00:35.734 --> 00:00:38.901
My parents raised two daughters
before me and then me,

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:39.968
and we were all raised --

00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.367
This was our
Mother Goose record.

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.634
-This is a hand-me-down.

00:00:43.634 --> 00:00:44.801
-A hand-me-down.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:46.100
-Yeah, it's been in
the family for years.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.400
-Right. Yes.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.901
And they're recorded by

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:53.567
Cyril Ritchard, Celeste Holm,
and Boris Karloff.

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.400
Boris Karloff, you know,

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:59.267
who famously played
Frankenstein's monster.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:01.601
-Yeah, I mean,
he's a very famous monster.

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.601
-And beautiful voice.

00:01:03.601 --> 00:01:07.434
But it's them
reading nursery rhymes

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:11.801
that are absolutely terrifying.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.534
-Now, we were talking,
and you go, "I gotta find it.

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.400
It's at home. I'll go home.
Next time, I'll bring it on."

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.534
And I go, "We'll find it."

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.000
We found it for you.
-But you have a whole --

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.367
-This is real.

00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:24.467
Now, this is Boris Karloff doing
"There was a Crooked Man."

00:01:24.467 --> 00:01:25.901
And you heard this as a child.

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:29.534
-Yeah, so listen to this and
imagine if you're 4-year-old.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:34.300
-He bought a crooked cat,
who caught a crooked mouse,

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:39.267
and they all lived together

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:44.367
in a little, crooked house.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:48.167
-Oh, my God.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.167 --> 00:01:52.367
-No! Wow! Wow!

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:54.000
-The temperature
just dropped over here.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:58.300
-"Little crooked --" Like,
"What are you doing, buddy?"

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:00.267
-It was like
an experiment, I think,

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.033
that my parents were conducting.

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:05.033
-Oh, my gosh.
-Congratulations, Questlove.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.534
-Oh, wow. Yeah. Yeah.
-I appreciate it.

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:10.634
-Questlove --
-Thank you.

00:02:10.634 --> 00:02:12.300
-He's amazing.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.801
-I want to talk about
"Blacklist,"

00:02:13.801 --> 00:02:15.534
because now you're in your
ninth season.

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:21.300
Yeah, you got cheers as
I'm talking about it earlier

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:23.667
in the show, because you're
just fantastic as Red.

00:02:23.667 --> 00:02:27.000
-We just got picked up
just this afternoon.

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:28.367
Word came out.

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.934
They -- Everyone was hustling
around to try and do it

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.067
so we could announce it
on the show.

00:02:32.067 --> 00:02:33.767
We just got picked up
for a 10th season.

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:37.200
-Come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.834
Well-deserved.

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:40.868
Wow!
10 seasons of "The Blacklist."

00:02:40.868 --> 00:02:41.868
-10 seasons.

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:43.234
-Again, I will say this.

00:02:43.234 --> 00:02:44.467
I say this every time
you come on.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.701
But when you watch
"The Blacklist,"

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:47.601
it doesn't look like --
It's not like a show.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.501
It's a movie
you are making every week.

00:02:49.501 --> 00:02:52.367
And it's explosions
and it's stuff.

00:02:52.367 --> 00:02:56.067
And it is work. It really is.
I mean, it's work.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:59.200
And the fact that you made this
also during the pandemic

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.567
and during COVID.

00:03:00.567 --> 00:03:05.300
-Yeah, no, it was really --
You know, we shut down

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.367
on March 13th of --
What the hell year was that?

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:10.367
-Yeah. We all erased it.
-'20, I guess.

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:12.400
-Yeah, 2020.
-Right? '20? Yeah.

00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:16.234
And we shut down on the 13th --
it was a Friday.

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:19.534
And we were in the middle
of Episode 19 of that season,

00:03:19.534 --> 00:03:25.133
and it became clear
we weren't coming back for

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.534
the last few episodes
of the season.

00:03:27.534 --> 00:03:32.634
So we decided, with 19,
we wanted to end with

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:35.467
some sort of satisfaction
for the viewers,

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:40.501
so we -- so they animated

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:43.033
the second half
of that Episode 19.

00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.200
And then we spent really the
rest of that summer,

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.167
during lockdown, trying
to discuss with Sony and NBC

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.601
and the producers,
other producers on the show,

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:54.000
how we can could back and how --

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.133
You know, what the
shape of that would be

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.567
and what the ramifications
would be and so on.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:04:02.868
So, that year, 2020,
we came back.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:09.801
And NBC and Sony --
great partners on this show --

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:14.033
they had ordered 22 episodes
for season -- for that year.

00:04:14.033 --> 00:04:16.434
And we shot all 22 episodes.

00:04:16.434 --> 00:04:19.100
We didn't shut down once,
all during the pandemic.

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:22.400
It was all really due
to this incredible effort

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.367
from our producers and --

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:26.934
-NBC does a great job here,
and I should props to

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:28.334
my crew and everybody,

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.834
the camera operators,
everybody here.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:34.734
Safely -- And doing it safely
and doing it right,

00:04:34.734 --> 00:04:37.634
because, well,
we all need entertainment.

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:39.000
-And the same this season, too,

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.834
with Omicron
and everything else.

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:42.467
We did not shut down once.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:43.968
We were able to do --
We're doing a full

00:04:43.968 --> 00:04:45.400
22 episodes this year.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.467
And we're gonna carry on
and do another one next year.

00:04:49.467 --> 00:04:50.534
-That's amazing. And that --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:55.501
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:55.501 --> 00:04:58.501
Here's James Spader in Friday's
episode of "The Blacklist."

00:04:58.501 --> 00:04:59.901
Take a look at this.

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:02.200
-Absolutely not.
-Come on. Harold --

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.234
-Hedwig Hawkins was caught
with over a million dollars

00:05:04.234 --> 00:05:05.767
worth of pirated soybeans.

00:05:05.767 --> 00:05:07.100
-Pirated?

00:05:07.100 --> 00:05:10.467
Heddie was just selling seeds
to farmers at a price.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:13.367
If my associate
is guilty of anything,

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:16.234
it's simply trying to
ease the economic strain

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:18.434
on the hard-working
men and women

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:22.167
who put the tofu in your turkey,
the cotton in your shirt,

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:24.667
the beans in your coffee.

00:05:24.667 --> 00:05:26.767
Everything it means to be human.

00:05:26.767 --> 00:05:28.634
-But our immunity agreement
is with you,

00:05:28.634 --> 00:05:29.834
not with your employees.

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.334
-If she talks,
it will be damaging.

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:35.901
How much is hard to tell,
but it would certainly have

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:39.133
repercussions for me
and for this task force.

00:05:39.133 --> 00:05:41.100
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:42.534
James Spader, everybody.

00:05:42.534 --> 00:05:46.300
"The Blacklist" airs
Fridays at 8:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:05:46.300 --> 00:05:49.467
Boris Karloff reads
Mother Goose,

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:50.968
available wherever
you can find it.

